<title>ITALY: TIM sees H1 96 pretax profit up 48 pct.</title>
<headline>TIM sees H1 96 pretax profit up 48 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ending June 30</p>
<p>(In billion lire unless stated)</p>
<p>    Cons pretax profit		  955    vs  up 48 pct</p>
<p>    Cons revenue			3,355    vs  2,800</p>
<p>NOTE - Italy's state-controlled mobile phone group Telecom Italian Mobile said the comparison figures were for the last 5-1/2 months of 1995, since a tranche of the group shares were only privatised in July 1995.</p>
<p>TIM said at September 18, its total mobile phone clients reached 4,777,807, of which 3,806,306 were for analogue models and 971,501 for GSM digital phones.  </p>
<p>    Gross operating margin	 1,537.9  vs 1,255.6</p>
<p>    Operating profit		   952.0  vs   681.6</p>
<p>    Pretax before extraordinaries  955.0  vs   645.6</p>
<p>    Pretax profit			955.1  vs   645.6</p>
<p>NOTE - TIM said its net debt at end-June 1996 was 526.9 billion lire compared to a debt at end-December 1995 of 323.0 lire.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129502</p>
</text>
